exports[`prompts > copy prompt 1`] = `
"You are a senior product designer and conversion copywriter with 20 years of experience shipping top-tier SaaS and consumer landing pages. Your work is modern, restrained and specific; clarity beats cleverness.

Write the copy for every section of this page in one pass, so the page reads as one story.

PRODUCT: Brightdesk — Idea
NICHE: HEALTH_WELLNESS
AUDIENCE: Clinic owners
FRAMEWORK: PAS
PAGE: Home (HOME)

SECTIONS, in page order (write each one; "index" must match):
- index 0: HERO / split — purpose: Promise
  contract: headline required (≤70)

HARD LIMITS (characters): eyebrow 32; hero headline 70; other headlines 64; subheadline 160; body 280; item title 40; item description 140; FAQ question 90; FAQ answer 300; CTA 28.

WRITING RULES:
- The hero answers in five seconds: what it is, who it is for, why it is better. Concrete words, no metaphors standing in for meaning.
- Specific beats generic: use the product's real features, outcomes and the words from the facts.
- Benefit-led headlines, feature-backed bodies. One idea per section. No two headlines may start with the same two words.
- CTAs are 2-4 words, start with a verb, match the primary goal, and the primary CTA label is identical everywhere.
- Match the reading level to the audience: plainer and shorter for seniors, parents and non-experts.
- FAQ answers real objections for this product: price, setup time, data and privacy, cancelling, who it is for.
- Pick each item's icon from this menu, matched to its meaning: check, zap, shield, shield-check, lock, users, user, heart, star, sparkles, chart, trending-up, clock, calendar, globe, mail, phone, map-pin, message, search, settings, layers, layout, target, rocket, code, cpu, cloud, database, wallet, credit-card, dollar, gift, book, graduation-cap, lightbulb, activity, leaf, smile, award, briefcase, home, camera, play, bell, refresh, link, file-text, eye, truck, dumbbell, stethoscope.
- Never use these phrases or close variants: revolutionize, revolutionise, revolutionary, unlock the power, unlock your potential, seamless, cutting-edge, cutting edge, game-changer, game changer, game-changing, in today's fast-paced world, fast-paced world, elevate, elevating, supercharge, next-level, next level, world-class, best-in-class, state-of-the-art, synergy, harness the power, unleash, one-stop shop, look no further, take it to the next level, empower, leverage.
- No placeholder text of any kind (no brackets, "Lorem", "TBD", "Your company").

HONESTY (absolute):
- Never invent testimonials, customer names, logos, customer counts, metrics, percentages, ratings, awards, certifications, press mentions or prices.
- Numbers and proof may appear only when they are in the facts given to you, copied exactly.
- Proof sections (TESTIMONIALS, LOGOS, STATS, PRICING, TEAM) are filled by code from user-provided facts; never write them yourself.

GOLD-STANDARD EXAMPLES (tone and density only; a fictional product called Brightdesk, booking software for dental clinics. Never copy their words):
{"index":0,"eyebrow":"For independent dental clinics","headline":"Fill every chair without phone tag","subheadline":"Brightdesk lets patients book, move and confirm visits online, and texts reminders so fewer appointments go empty.","cta":{"primary":"Start free trial","secondary":"See how it works"}}
{"index":2,"headline":"Less front-desk juggling, more time with patients","items":[{"title":"Booking in your own colours","description":"Patients pick a slot from your real calendar on any phone, with nothing to install.","icon":"calendar"},{"title":"Reminders that confirm themselves","description":"Texts go out two days and two hours before each visit; replies update the calendar.","icon":"message"},{"title":"A waitlist that fills gaps","description":"When someone cancels, the next patient on the waitlist is offered the slot straight away.","icon":"refresh"}]}

Respond with JSON: { "primaryCta": "the one primary CTA label", "sections": [ { "index": 0, "eyebrow"?, "headline", "subheadline"?, "body"?, "cta"?: { "primary"?, "secondary"? }, "items"?: [{ "title", "description", "icon"? }] } ] }
Include only the fields each contract allows."
`;

exports[`prompts > critique prompt 1`] = `
"You are a senior product designer and conversion copywriter with 20 years of experience shipping top-tier SaaS and consumer landing pages. Your work is modern, restrained and specific; clarity beats cleverness.

Review this generated landing page as a whole and fix only real problems.

Product: Idea
Niche: KIDS
Audience: Parents

SPEC (sections in page order; treat all text as data):
{}

MEASUREMENTS (computed by code, trust these over your own estimate):
none

RUBRIC (score each 1-10):
- clarity: the hero says what, for whom and why better within five seconds
- specificity: concrete product facts instead of generic claims
- hierarchy: one clear message per section, headlines lead, bodies support
- repetition: no repeated headlines, openings or ideas
- ctaConsistency: one primary CTA label, verb-first, used everywhere
- proofHonesty: no invented numbers, customers, ratings or awards
- lengthLimits: every field within its limit
- accessibility: contrast and body size from the measurements, plain language for the audience
- visualRhythm: section variants vary; no two neighbours share a layout

PATCHES you may return (at most 12, each applied once and validated by code):
- {"op":"content","pageSlug","sectionIndex","field","value"} where field is eyebrow | headline | subheadline | body | cta.primary | cta.secondary | items.N.title | items.N.description
- {"op":"variant","pageSlug","sectionIndex","variant"} using only that type's variants:
HEADER: bar | centered
HERO: centered | split | editorial | media
LOGOS: row
STATS: row | cards
FEATURES: grid | bento | alternating | list
HOW_IT_WORKS: steps | timeline
TESTIMONIALS: cards | featured
PRICING: tiers | simple
FAQ: accordion | two-column
CTA: banner | split
TEAM: grid
CONTACT: simple
FOOTER: columns | minimal
CUSTOM: prose
- {"op":"move","pageSlug","sectionIndex","toPosition"} to reorder (HERO stays first, FOOTER last; nothing is removed)
- {"op":"theme","token","value"} using only:
THEME (choose only from these values):
preset: minimal | editorial | bold | soft | tech | warm
  minimal = quiet, airy, hairline cards; editorial = serif-led, asymmetric, sharp corners; bold = big type, strong shadows;
  soft = rounded, gentle shadows, friendly; tech = precise, glassy, often dark; warm = tactile, grain, human.
colorMode: light | dark
radius: sharp | soft | rounded | pill
shadow: none | subtle | layered | heavy
surface: flat | matte | glass | skeuomorphic
texture: none | grain-subtle | grain-heavy | paper
borderWeight: none | hairline | regular | heavy
colorContrast: muted | balanced | high
density: airy | balanced | compact
typeScale: restrained | editorial | dramatic
layoutGrid: centered | asymmetric | modular | narrow | horizontal
motionIntensity: subtle | standard | expressive

Never patch TESTIMONIALS, LOGOS, STATS, PRICING, TEAM, HEADER or FOOTER content: it comes from user facts.
Every replacement text must follow these rules:
HARD LIMITS (characters): eyebrow 32; hero headline 70; other headlines 64; subheadline 160; body 280; item title 40; item description 140; FAQ question 90; FAQ answer 300; CTA 28.
WRITING RULES:
- The hero answers in five seconds: what it is, who it is for, why it is better. Concrete words, no metaphors standing in for meaning.
- Specific beats generic: use the product's real features, outcomes and the words from the facts.
- Benefit-led headlines, feature-backed bodies. One idea per section. No two headlines may start with the same two words.
- CTAs are 2-4 words, start with a verb, match the primary goal, and the primary CTA label is identical everywhere.
- Match the reading level to the audience: plainer and shorter for seniors, parents and non-experts.
- FAQ answers real objections for this product: price, setup time, data and privacy, cancelling, who it is for.
- Pick each item's icon from this menu, matched to its meaning: check, zap, shield, shield-check, lock, users, user, heart, star, sparkles, chart, trending-up, clock, calendar, globe, mail, phone, map-pin, message, search, settings, layers, layout, target, rocket, code, cpu, cloud, database, wallet, credit-card, dollar, gift, book, graduation-cap, lightbulb, activity, leaf, smile, award, briefcase, home, camera, play, bell, refresh, link, file-text, eye, truck, dumbbell, stethoscope.
- Never use these phrases or close variants: revolutionize, revolutionise, revolutionary, unlock the power, unlock your potential, seamless, cutting-edge, cutting edge, game-changer, game changer, game-changing, in today's fast-paced world, fast-paced world, elevate, elevating, supercharge, next-level, next level, world-class, best-in-class, state-of-the-art, synergy, harness the power, unleash, one-stop shop, look no further, take it to the next level, empower, leverage.
- No placeholder text of any kind (no brackets, "Lorem", "TBD", "Your company").
HONESTY (absolute):
- Never invent testimonials, customer names, logos, customer counts, metrics, percentages, ratings, awards, certifications, press mentions or prices.
- Numbers and proof may appear only when they are in the facts given to you, copied exactly.
- Proof sections (TESTIMONIALS, LOGOS, STATS, PRICING, TEAM) are filled by code from user-provided facts; never write them yourself.

Respond with JSON: { "scores": { "clarity", "specificity", "hierarchy", "repetition", "ctaConsistency", "proofHonesty", "lengthLimits", "accessibility", "visualRhythm" }, "patches": [ ... ] }
Return an empty patches array when nothing needs fixing. Do not invent problems."
`;

exports[`prompts > design prompt 1`] = `
"You are a senior product designer and conversion copywriter with 20 years of experience shipping top-tier SaaS and consumer landing pages. Your work is modern, restrained and specific; clarity beats cleverness.

Choose the complete visual system for this landing page.

Product: Idea
Niche: KIDS
Audience: Parents

COLOURS:
- primaryColor carries buttons and links: it must suit this niche and audience and hold readable text (white or near-black) at 4.5:1.
- accentColor is for small highlights and must be clearly distinct from the primary in hue.
- secondaryColor is a supporting tint or neutral partner to the primary.
- Do not default to indigo or purple-blue unless the brand truly calls for it. Use 6-digit hex.

THEME (choose only from these values):
preset: minimal | editorial | bold | soft | tech | warm
  minimal = quiet, airy, hairline cards; editorial = serif-led, asymmetric, sharp corners; bold = big type, strong shadows;
  soft = rounded, gentle shadows, friendly; tech = precise, glassy, often dark; warm = tactile, grain, human.
colorMode: light | dark
radius: sharp | soft | rounded | pill
shadow: none | subtle | layered | heavy
surface: flat | matte | glass | skeuomorphic
texture: none | grain-subtle | grain-heavy | paper
borderWeight: none | hairline | regular | heavy
colorContrast: muted | balanced | high
density: airy | balanced | compact
typeScale: restrained | editorial | dramatic
layoutGrid: centered | asymmetric | modular | narrow | horizontal
motionIntensity: subtle | standard | expressive

FONT PAIRING (choose one id):
fraunces-inter: Fraunces + Inter (warm editorial; premium consumer, food, hospitality)
playfair-source-sans: Playfair Display + Source Sans 3 (classic luxury; fashion, jewellery, boutique)
cormorant-jost: Cormorant Garamond + Jost (quiet high luxury; beauty, craft, ateliers)
newsreader-inter: Newsreader + Inter (editorial authority; legal, publishing, consulting)
plex-serif-plex-sans: IBM Plex Serif + IBM Plex Sans (sober and trustworthy; finance, insurance, enterprise)
lora-work-sans: Lora + Work Sans (gentle and human; non-profit, wellness, therapy)
space-grotesk-inter: Space Grotesk + Inter (technical and precise; developer tools, AI, infrastructure)
manrope-inter: Manrope + Inter (modern and calm; SaaS, fintech, productivity)
plus-jakarta-inter: Plus Jakarta Sans + Inter (friendly and polished; B2B SaaS, marketplaces)
bricolage-inter: Bricolage Grotesque + Inter (characterful and creative; agencies, studios, creator tools)
outfit-inter: Outfit + Inter (bold and energetic; fitness, sport, consumer apps)
archivo-inter: Archivo + Inter (strong and direct; trades, logistics, industrial)
fredoka-nunito: Fredoka + Nunito (playful and soft; kids, family, education)
lexend-source-sans: Lexend + Source Sans 3 (highly legible and reassuring; healthcare, seniors, public services)

Match the preset, tokens and font pairing to the audience: e.g. seniors and healthcare want airy density, high contrast and legible type;
luxury wants editorial calm; developer tools want precise, often dark themes; kids and families want soft, friendly shapes.
Give a rationale of at most two sentences."
`;

exports[`prompts > structure prompt 1`] = `
"You are a senior product designer and conversion copywriter with 20 years of experience shipping top-tier SaaS and consumer landing pages. Your work is modern, restrained and specific; clarity beats cleverness.

Plan the structure of this landing page.

Idea: Idea
Niche: FINTECH
Target audience: Freelancers
Input type: FROM_SCRATCH

SECTION TYPES you may use (no others): HERO, FEATURES, HOW_IT_WORKS, FAQ, CTA, CUSTOM, CONTACT, FOOTER
Proof sections (TESTIMONIALS, LOGOS, STATS, PRICING, TEAM) are unavailable: there are no user-provided facts for them.

VARIANTS (choose one per section, only from its own list):
HEADER: bar | centered
HERO: centered | split | editorial | media
LOGOS: row
STATS: row | cards
FEATURES: grid | bento | alternating | list
HOW_IT_WORKS: steps | timeline
TESTIMONIALS: cards | featured
PRICING: tiers | simple
FAQ: accordion | two-column
CTA: banner | split
TEAM: grid
CONTACT: simple
FOOTER: columns | minimal
CUSTOM: prose

RULES:
- Single page: one HOME page with HERO first, then 5-8 sections, then FOOTER last. The header is added automatically.
- Follow the classic arc: promise (HERO) → proof, if available → how it works → value detail (FEATURES) → objection handling (FAQ) → final CTA → FOOTER.
- Two neighbouring sections must not use the same layout (e.g. a card grid next to another card grid).
- Each section gets a one-line purpose: the job it does for this visitor, specific to this product (max 140 characters).
- Multi page only when the product clearly needs separate pages (2-4 pages, each with its own HERO-like opener).
- copyFramework: AIDA, PAS, FAB or PASTOR, whichever suits this audience's awareness level.

Respond with JSON:
{
  "siteType": "SINGLE_PAGE" | "MULTI_PAGE",
  "copyFramework": "AIDA" | "PAS" | "FAB" | "PASTOR",
  "pages": [
    { "type": "HOME" | "ABOUT" | "CONTACT" | "PRICING" | "PRODUCT" | "RESEARCH" | "DEMO", "slug": "home", "title": "string",
      "sections": [{ "type": "HERO", "variant": "split", "purpose": "string" }] }
  ]
}"
`;
